A1. A lady of the east side. ~ SKIRT
A6. This comes after an old-fashioned Christmas Eve party. ~ CHRISTMAS
A14. Something trousers should be kept in. ~ PRESS
A16. This goes up in the air over radios. ~ AERIAL
A18. Decree. ~ ENACT
A20. You can get quite a kick out of this. ~ PINT
A21. Preposition. ~ TO
A22. Something aviators like to keep. ~ UP
A24. Something Scotchmen don't do. ~ TREAT
A26. Salted Geraniums (init.). ~ SG
A27. French coin. ~ SOU
A28. What gamblers have to do if they want to win a bet. ~ BET
A30. Slink. ~ SNEAK
A32. Proboscis, horn or beezer. ~ SNOUT
A34. Girl's name. ~ EDNA
A36. This borders on the humerus. ~ ELBOW
A38. Parts of circles. ~ ARCS
A39. A volcano in Sicily. ~ ETNA
A41. A deep sleep. ~ SOPOR
A43. Exclamation of the hard of hearing. ~ EH
A44. To die (Scot.). ~ DEE
A46. Vender of bananas and shoe shines. ~ WOP
A48. Transpose (abbr.). ~ TR
A50. What follows when you strike a match? ~ FLARE
A53. A guy. ~ BOZO
A55. Eats. ~ GRUB
A57. Position of an unsuccessful prize fighter. ~ INERT
A59. This is often painted red. ~ TOWN
A61. What a plumber does when he gets up at seven o'clock. ~ RISES
A63. The kind of a hill that flivvers regret. ~ STEEP
A65. This number of wives is one too many. ~ ONE
A66. Something girls would rather do than go fishing. ~ EAT
A67. Plural pronoun. ~ WE
A69. Many a Puritan lost his head when his redskinned brother insisted on taking this kind of a souvenir home. ~ SCALP
A71. Senior (abbr.). ~ SR
A72. Half of a printer's measure. ~ EN
A73. What lawyers match for a living. ~ WITS
A75. Same as twenty-four horizontal. ~ TREAT
A77. Something doctors use to draw things out of their patients (sing.). ~ PINCER
A79. What men become after they get over falling in love. ~ SANER
A81. These chickens have long necks. ~ SHANGHAIS
A82. Thirteen to nineteen. ~ TEENS

D2. Kitchén police (init.). ~ KP
D3. Cause and effect of cross words. ~ IRE
D4. Something landlords can raise much easier than their tenants can. ~ RENT
D5. In Russia these are big cheeses. ~ TSARS
D7. The villain speaks! ~ HA
D8. A difficult thing to live up to (abbr.). ~ REP
D9. This goes around a pupil. ~ IRIS
D10. What a man does when he's taking a bath and there's no lock on the door. ~ SINGS
D11. What old ladies do when they want some tatting. ~ TAT
D12. One thousand and fifty. ~ ML
