D15. What a wife makes if she can't buy a new hat. ~ SCENE
D17. Something people squeeze to get pasted in the jaw. ~ TUBE
D19. Chinese seventy-five cent pieces. ~ TAELS
D21. What football players play for. ~ TOUCHDOWNS
D23. This fellow knows what a "quick turnover" means. ~ PEDESTRIAN
D25. A stool or small cushioned seat (pl.). ~ TABOURETS
D27. What a run-down pedestrian gets. ~ SORE
D29. People go all to pieces over this (abbr.). ~ TNT
D31. A Ku Klux policeman. ~ KOP
D33. A continent (abbr.). ~ NA
